cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I play the Bergen/Hardy style of 2/1 which I think is best. That means if I rebid 2@S that promises 6 and if I have no other suit to bid I make the default bid of 2N with only 5 spades. Some play that 2@S is the default bid and does not promise 6. But I think that makes things very awkward so I strongly recommend you play the Bergen style of 2/1.|
PG| ***** 48 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North's |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dummypoints,Bergen Dummy Points ^*N|CP||FP||at| are 13 HCP, plus 1 length point, 1 quality suit point, and 1 point for the doubleton heart for 16 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dummypoints,Bergen Dummy Points ^*N|CP||FP||at|. It perhaps is enough to try for slam although close and turns out 4@S is the best spot.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 49 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|A 4@S bid is known as ^*BFast Arrival^*n. We are in a game forcing auction. So if North jumps to 4@S he is showing a minimum game forcing hand with no slam interest whereas if he bids 3@S, he is showing at least some slam interest.|
