UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The hand cannot be defeated. I think the line of play was reasonable as was the defense. However, after winning the @CA, the heart play had risks. North knows West has the @HJ (because with QJ South would have played the @HJ not the @HQ). |
PG| ***** 78 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So the second heart lead is risky, because if West holds the @H8 then that gives away another trick, which, as you can see, it did. However West always has 7 tricks (3 diamonds, 3 clubs, and 1 heart) so the hand cannot be defeated.

|
PG| ***** 79 ***** |


