mb|P|mb|P|mb|1D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I am not a big believer in opening light at the 1-level in 3rd seat. I like to use the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule Of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| in all seats. Further, I love to preempt in 3rd seat but prefer to use |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule Of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| so partner does not have to worry about whether or not I have a real opening bid. Many better players disagree with me.|
PG| ***** 81 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|On this hand, I do have 12 HCP and 4-4 in the majors so it appears to meet the rule of 20. However, I use "Bergen Adjusted Points" to calculate my points, so I technically should subtract 1 for Qx of clubs. |
PG| ***** 82 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That means my hand is worth only 11 points and does not meet the Rule 0f 20. But since I am 4-4 in the majors and can therefore compete effectively, I will cheat a bit an open the hand. 
|
PG| ***** 83 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
mb|1S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|1@S bid by West is a good bid. West has 17 points but suit, Spades here, are not strong enough for double and correct. However, sometimes you can and should double and correct, though you run the risk of not being able to bid your suit if the opponents interfere as they do here.|
